  "notes": "COMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {予想|よそう}に{反|はん}する (contrary to expectations)\n- {法律|ほうりつ}に{反|はん}する (violate the law)\n- {規則|きそく}に{反|はん}する (violate the rules)\n- {常識|じょうしき}に{反|はん}する (go against common sense)\n- {意|い}に{反|はん}する (against one's will)\n\nUSAGE:\nAlways takes the particle に to mark what is being contradicted or violated. The pattern ～に{反|はん}して is commonly used as a connective phrase meaning \"contrary to ~.\" For example, {予想|よそう}に{反|はん}して (contrary to expectations). The noun form {反|はん}する is a する verb but is almost always intransitive.",
